---@field preProvisioningToken? string Optional. Must and can only be set for Chrome OS devices.
---@field simlockProfileId? string Optional. Must and can only be set when DeviceProvisioningSectionType is SECTION_TYPE_SIM_LOCK. The unique identifier of the SimLock profile.
---@field deviceIdentifier? gcp.androiddeviceprovisioning_v1.DeviceIdentifier Required. Required. Device identifier of the device.
---@field googleWorkspaceCustomerId? string The Google Workspace customer ID.
---@field sectionType? gcp.androiddeviceprovisioning_v1.PartnerClaimSectionTypeEnum|string Required. The section type of the device's provisioning record.
---@field deviceMetadata? gcp.androiddeviceprovisioning_v1.DeviceMetadata Required. The metadata to attach to the device at claim.
---@field customerId? string The ID of the customer for whom the device is being claimed.
---@field configurationId? string Optional. The ID of the configuration applied to the device section.

---@alias gcp.androiddeviceprovisioning_v1.PartnerClaimList gcp.androiddeviceprovisioning_v1.PartnerClaim[]

---@alias gcp.androiddeviceprovisioning_v1.PartnerClaimSectionTypeEnum "SECTION_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SECTION_TYPE_SIM_LOCK"|"SECTION_TYPE_ZERO_TOUCH"

---Identifies one unclaim request.
---@class gcp.androiddeviceprovisioning_v1.PartnerUnclaim
---@field vacationModeExpireTime? string Optional. The expiration time of the vacation unlock.
---@field deviceIdentifier? gcp.androiddeviceprovisioning_v1.DeviceIdentifier Required. Device identifier of the device.
---@field sectionType? gcp.androiddeviceprovisioning_v1.PartnerUnclaimSectionTypeEnum|string Required. The section type of the device's provisioning record.
---@field deviceId? string Required. Device ID of the device.
---@field vacationModeDays? number Optional. The duration of the vacation unlock starting from when the request is processed. (1 day is treated as 24 hours)

---@alias gcp.androiddeviceprovisioning_v1.PartnerUnclaimList gcp.androiddeviceprovisioning_v1.PartnerUnclaim[]

---@alias gcp.androiddeviceprovisioning_v1.PartnerUnclaimSectionTypeEnum "SECTION_TYPE_UNSPECIFIED"|"SECTION_TYPE_SIM_LOCK"|"SECTION_TYPE_ZERO_TOUCH"

---@class gcp.androiddeviceprovisioning_v1.PatchCustomersConfigurationsRequest
---@field contactPhone? string Required. The telephone number that device users can call, using another device, to get help. Zero-touch enrollment shows this number to device users before device provisioning. Accepts numerals, spaces, the plus sign, hyphens, and parentheses.
---@field isDefault? boolean Required. Whether this is the default configuration that zero-touch enrollment applies to any new devices the organization purchases in the future. Only one customer configuration can be the default. Setting this value to `true`, changes the previous default configuration's `isDefault` value to `false`.
---@field contactEmail? string Required. The email address that device users can contact to get help. Zero-touch enrollment shows this email address to device users before device provisioning. The value is validated on input.
---@field customMessage? string A message, containing one or two sentences, to help device users get help or give them more details about what’s happening to their device. Zero-touch enrollment shows this message before the device is provisioned.
---@field configurationId? string Output only. The ID of the configuration. Assigned by the server.
---@field dpcResourcePath? string Required. The resource name of the selected DPC (device policy controller) in the format `customers/[CUSTOMER_ID]/dpcs/*`. To list the supported DPCs, call `customers.dpcs.list`.
---@field configurationName? string Required. A short name that describes the configuration's purpose. For example, _Sales team_ or _Temporary employees_. The zero-touch enrollment portal displays this name to IT admins.
---@field forcedResetTime? string Optional. The timeout before forcing factory reset the device if the device doesn't go through provisioning in the setup wizard, usually due to lack of network connectivity during setup wizard. Ranges from 0-6 hours, with 2 hours being the default if unset.
---@field companyName? string Required. The name of the organization. Zero-touch enrollment shows this organization name to device users during device provisioning.
---@field dpcExtras? string The JSON-formatted EMM provisioning extras that are passed to the DPC.
---@field updateMask? string Required. The field mask applied to the target `Configuration` before updating the fields. To learn more about using field masks, read [FieldMask](/protocol-buffers/docs/reference/google.protobuf#fieldmask) in the Protocol Buffers documentation.
---@field name string Output only. The API resource name in the format `customers/[CUSTOMER_ID]/configurations/[CONFIGURATION_ID]`. Assigned by the server.

---@class gcp.androiddeviceprovisioning_v1.RemoveConfigurationCustomersDevicesRequest
---@field device? gcp.androiddeviceprovisioning_v1.DeviceReference Required. The device to remove the configuration from. There are custom validations in RemoveConfigurationRequestValidator
---@field parent string Required. The customer managing the device in the format `customers/[CUSTOMER_ID]`.

